  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- A4. Exact LR-symmetric Q-solver ----\n   Imposes the four Baxter equations on Q1..Q4 together with the two dual equations,\n   with LR symmetry Q^4 = Q1 (twist 1/z1) and Q^3 = Q2 (twist 1/z2) -- exactly the\n   reference notebook's solveQsLR, but solved exactly rather than by NSolve.\n   Returns one association per state: the monic polynomial parts p[1..4] and the\n   integrals of motion. Q_i(u) = zz[i]^(-I u) p_i(u). *)\nClearAll[solveQsLR];\nsolveQsLR[L_, {M_, S_, Nn_}] := solveQsLR[L, {M, S, Nn}] = Module[\n  {exps, pf, vars, eqs, sols},\n  exps = {M, S - M, L + Nn - S, L - Nn};\n  If[Min[exps] < 0, Return[{}]];\n  pf[i_] := Function[uu, Evaluate[uu^exps[[i]] + Sum[c[k][i] uu^k, {k, 0, exps[[i]] - 1}]]];\n  vars = Join[Table[J1[b], {b, L - 1}], Table[J2[b], {b, 2 L - 1}], Table[J3[b], {b, L - 1}],\n              Flatten@Table[c[k][i], {i, 4}, {k, 0, exps[[i]] - 1}]];\n  eqs = Flatten@Join[\n     Table[CoefficientList[Expand@Together@BaxP[L, {M, S, Nn}][zz[i], pf[i]][u], u], {i, 4}],\n     {CoefficientList[Expand@Together@dBaxP[L, {M, S, Nn}][zz[4], pf[1]][u], u],\n      CoefficientList[Expand@Together@dBaxP[L, {M, S, Nn}][zz[3], pf[2]][u], u]}];\n  sols = Solve[Thread[Numerator[Together[eqs]] == 0], vars];\n  Association[\n     \"cfg\" -> {M, S, Nn}, \"L\" -> L, \"exps\" -> exps,\n     \"p\" -> Table[Simplify[pf[i][u] /. #], {i, 4}],\n     \"J\" -> Simplify[{Table[J1[b], {b, L - 1}], Table[J2[b], {b, 2 L - 1}],\n                      Table[J3[b], {b, L - 1}]} /. #]] & /@ sols];\n\n(* smoke test: the paper's L=2 [1,0,1] state is {M,S,Nn} = {0,1,0}, exps = {0,1,1,2} *)\nsolL2101 = solveQsLR[2, {0, 1, 0}];\n{Length[solL2101], First[solL2101][\"exps\"], #[\"p\"] & /@ solL2101}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
