  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## B. The FSoV norm `B` (eq. (12))\n\nRows `(alpha,j,k)`, columns `(beta,a,b)` with `j in {1,2}`, `k in {3,4}`, `a,b = +-1`,\n`alpha,beta = 1..L` -- an `8x8` determinant at `L=2`.\n\nLR symmetry gives `Q^3 = Q2`, `Q^4 = Q1`, so with `m = 5-k` in `{1,2}`:\n\n```\nQ_j^[a](u) Q^k[b](u) = e^((phi_j + phi_m) u) * z_j^(a/2) z_m^(b/2)\n                       * p_j(u + a i/2) p_m(u + b i/2)\n```\n\nEverything is switched to phase variables `z_k = Exp[I phi_k]` here, because the twist\nenters the bracket only through `e^((phi_j+phi_m) u)` and the half-shifts need `z^(a/2)`.\nThe Q-solving stayed rational in `z1,z2`; only the bracket needs phases.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- B1. FSoV bracket (16) and phase-variable state data ---- *)\nClearAll[brk, ph, zof, pph, Q12f, stateData];\n(* <f>_{ell,alpha}: contour encircles the order-ell poles at u = +-i/2 counterclockwise *)\nbrk[f_, ell_, alpha_] := Module[{g},\n  g = Exp[2 Pi u (alpha - 1)] f/((u + I/2)^ell (u - I/2)^ell);\n  2 Pi I/(-2 Pi)^alpha (Residue[g, {u, I/2}] + Residue[g, {u, -I/2}])];\n\nph[1] = ph1; ph[2] = ph2; ph[3] = -ph2; ph[4] = -ph1;\nzof[k_] := Exp[I ph[k]];\n\n(* load a state: polynomial parts p_1..p_4 rewritten in phase variables *)\nstateData[st_] := (pph[i_] := pph[i] = Simplify[st[\"p\"][[i]] /. {zz[1] -> zof[1], zz[2] -> zof[2]}]);\n\nClearAll[pph];\nstateData[solL2101[[2]]];   (* the paper's (P1) state *)\n{pph[1], pph[2]} // Simplify",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"673673\" data-output-id=\"5\" data-out-n=\"34\" data-sub-idx=\"10\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"6\" data-sub-start=\"15\" data-sub-end=\"15\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[34]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"19\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:3em;vertical-align:-1.25em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size4\">{</span></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.59em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7751em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.989em;margin-right:0.05