  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## C. Staged untwisting\n\nEmpirical findings so far, for the paper's `L=2`, `[1,0,1]` state (`{M,S,Nn}={0,1,0}`,\n`lambda = {0,1,1,2}`), which is an su(2)-sector state (`M = Nn = 0`):\n\n**Step 1 (`phi1 -> 0`, `phi2` fixed).** Exactly one row of the 8x8 matrix,\n`(alpha,j,k) = (1,1,4)` -- the `alpha=1` row of the `Q1 Q1` block -- vanishes identically\nat `z1 = 1` (corank 1). Its vanishing order in `phi1` is `2L - lambda_j - lambdabar_k - beta\n= 4 - beta`, i.e. Appendix N's law applied per block. The `alpha=2` row of the same block\nvanishes as `phi1^1` in the `beta=2` columns. Min-cost permutation gives\n`det M = O(phi1^2)`, confirmed numerically.\n\n**Step 2 (`phi2 -> 0`).** Entries now *diverge* (orders down to `phi2^-2`), and the naive\nmin-cost permutation predicts `phi2^-2` while the true order is `phi2^12` -- **14 orders of\ncancellation**. The limit is therefore not computable entrywise; good linear combinations\nare mandatory.\n\nThe rotation is fixed by the worst entry `(2,2,3)` at `beta=1`, which is quadratic in `r`:\n`E(2,2,3) + r (E(2,1,3) + E(2,2,4)) + r^2 E(2,1,4)`, with leading coefficients\n`2I`, `-4I`, `2I` -- i.e. `2I (c-1)^2` for `r = c/phi2`. Double root at `c = 1`:\n\n```\nr = 1/phi2 ,    Q2t = Q2 + Q1/phi2 ,    Q2hat = lim (Q2t/phi2) = u^2/2 + 1/3\n```\n\nThis is exactly \"subtract the divergent multiple of Q1\": at `z1=1` the state has\n`p2 = u - Cot[phi2]`, so `Q2 -> -Q1/phi2` as `phi2 -> 0`. Note the degree jumps from\n`lambda_2 = 1` to 2.\n\nSince `det H = 1`, `Q12` and hence `B` are literally unchanged by the rotation.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- C1. Matrix builder for arbitrary Q1, Q2 (not necessarily z^(-I u) * poly) ----\n   LR symmetry: Q^4 = Q1, Q^3 = Q2, so the (j,k) entry uses Q_j and Q_(5-k). *)\nClearAll[mkEnt, mkM, mkQ12, mkB];\nmkEnt[QF_, alpha_, j_, k_, beta_, a_, b_] :=\n  brk[(QF[j] /. u -> u + a I/2) u^(beta - 1) (QF[5 - k] /. u -> u + b I/2), LL, alpha];\nmkM[QF_] := Table[mkEnt[QF, rr[[1]], rr[[2]], rr[[3]], cc[[1]], cc[[2]], cc[[3]]],\n                  {rr, rowsIdx}, {cc, colsIdx}];\nmkQ12[QF_, uu_] := (QF[1] /. u -> uu + I/2) (QF[2] /. u -> uu - I/2)\n                 - (QF[1] /. u -> uu - I/2) (QF[2] /. u -> uu + I/2);\nmkB[QF_] := Det[mkM[QF]]/(mkQ12[QF, -I/2] (-mkQ12[QF, I/2]))^(2 LL);\n\n(* original basis *)\nQorig[i_] := Exp[ph[i] u] pph[i];\n(* duality-rotated basis, det H = 1 *)\nQrot[1] := Qorig[1]; Qrot[2] := Qorig[2] + Qorig[1]/ph2;\n\n(* B is unchanged by the rotation, and Q12 is too *)\ntestpt = {ph1 -> 1/3, ph2 -> 1/7};\n{N[mkB[Qorig] /. testpt, 20], N[mkB[Qrot] /. testpt, 20],\n N[(mkQ12[Qorig, I/2] - mkQ12[Qrot, I/2]) /. testpt, 20]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
