  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## D. Result: closed formula for the `L=2` norm\n\nStaged limit (`phi1 -> 0` first, then `phi2 -> 0`), for `{M,S,Nn} = {0,1,0}`:\n\n```\nB  ->  phi1^2 phi2^4 * (-4) * Bsu2untw ,      Bsu2untw = 8\n```\n\nwhere `Bsu2untw` is built **entirely from untwisted Q-functions**:\n\n```\n              det_{1<=alpha,beta<=L} < Q12hat u^(beta-1) Q12hat >_{L,alpha}\nBsu2untw  =  -----------------------------------------------------------------\n                        ( Q12hat(i/2) Q12hat(-i/2) )^L\n\nQ1hat = 1 ,   Q2hat = u^2/2 + 1/3 ,   Q12hat = Q1hat^+ Q2hat^- - Q1hat^- Q2hat^+ = -I u\n```\n\nThe untwisted `Q2hat` is *not* the naive limit of `Q2` (which diverges); it is the\nduality-rotated combination `lim (Q2 + Q1/phi2)/phi2`, and its degree is 2, not\n`lambda_2 = 1`.\n\nChecks performed:\n- `Q`-solver reproduces the paper's (P1) exactly (solution 2 of `solveQsLR[2,{0,1,0}]`).\n- `B` is numerically invariant under `Q2 -> Q2 + r Q1` to 20+ digits, and `Q12` is\n  unchanged identically -- the rotation is pure gauge, as Appendix D requires.\n- `Bsu2`, the Appendix-L su(2) determinant built from the *twisted* `Q12`, tends to the\n  same value 8 as the untwisted-`Q` expression.\n- `B1/phi2^4 -> -32 = -4 * 8`, confirmed to 6 digits.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- D1. Final numbers and checks ---- *)\nresults = <|\n  \"step1 order in phi1\" -> 2,\n  \"step2 order in phi2\" -> 4,\n  \"rotation r\" -> 1/ph2,\n  \"Q1hat\" -> 1,\n  \"Q2hat\" -> Limit[(Qorig[2] + Qorig[1]/ph2)/ph2 /. ph1 -> 0, ph2 -> 0],\n  \"Q12hat\" -> Q12hat,\n  \"Bsu2untw (untwisted Qs)\" -> Simplify[Bsu2untw],\n  \"Bsu2 twisted, phi2->0\" -> Limit[Bsu2, ph2 -> 0],\n  \"lim B1/phi2^4\" -> N[(B1/ph2^4) /. ph2 -> 1/800, 12],\n  \"predicted -4*Bsu2untw\" -> -4 Simplify[Bsu2untw]|>",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
